such that #f −1 (t) ≤ m for all t ∈ [k]. Similarly, let Surm (n, k) be the set of m-surjective
functions, that is, f : [n] → [k] such that #f −1 (t) ≥ m for all t ∈ [k]. Note that injec-
tive functions are 1-injections and surjective functions are 1-surjections. We also define the
statistic ηj (f ) = #f −1 ({j}).
Theorem 2.3 ([9, Theorem 2.11]). Fix F to be either Injm (n, k) or Sur1 (n, k) for given
n, k, m ∈ P. Then under the action of w = wn ◦ wn−1 ◦ · · · ◦ w1 on F, ηj is nk -mesic for any
j ∈ [k].
This result is conjectured to hold for Surm (n, k), but is still open for m > 1. Proof details
can be found in Sections 2.2–2.4 of [9].
